WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.218
Meet wcrew — a shift roster co-pilot where
a café manager and a browser agent fix

2
00:00:03.298 --> 00:00:06.387
next week’s schedule together.

3
00:00:06.387 --> 00:00:09.682
For the independent shop that still builds
the roster on Sunday night.

4
00:00:09.794 --> 00:00:14.338
Rostering is eight constraints at once:
skills, availability, minors’ curfew,

5
00:00:14.418 --> 00:00:18.883
eleven hours rest, ten hours a day, five
consecutive days, lead coverage, overtime

6
00:00:18.963 --> 00:00:23.428
at one-point-five, preferences, and a
fifty-two hundred dollar budget.

7
00:00:23.428 --> 00:00:25.219
Managers balance fairness.

8
00:00:25.219 --> 00:00:26.724
Agents balance speed.

9
00:00:26.724 --> 00:00:28.736
Together they’re better than either alone.

10
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.324
Perfect for WebMCP.

11
00:00:30.324 --> 00:00:33.623
Instead of an agent guessing through a
dense grid, the site exposes fifteen typed

12
00:00:33.703 --> 00:00:36.923
tools on document dot modelContext.

13
00:00:36.923 --> 00:00:41.362
The agent acts inside your live,
authenticated tab — not a shadow backend.

14
00:00:41.362 --> 00:00:45.155
Every change is observable, attributable,
and undoable.

15
00:00:45.155 --> 00:00:46.819
That’s the trust contract.

16
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.823
This is wcrew dot pages dot dev. Rosewater
Coffee, Wharf Street.

17
00:00:50.823 --> 00:00:52.972
Thirty-nine shifts, ten staff.

18
00:00:52.972 --> 00:00:55.838
Left: the team with skills, contracted
hours, and an untrusted note canary in

19
00:00:55.917 --> 00:00:58.704
Inés’s profile.

20
00:00:58.704 --> 00:01:01.956
Center: the week board — dashed cards are
open.

21
00:01:01.956 --> 00:01:05.959
Top: coverage, labour cost with overtime,
and the publish gate.

22
00:01:05.959 --> 00:01:10.069
Right: compliance, cost breakdown, and the
actor-tagged activity feed.

23
00:01:10.177 --> 00:01:13.543
We ship with seeded errors so the first
agent call finds something real: Kofi

24
00:01:13.623 --> 00:01:16.909
double-booked Thursday on bake and bar,
Maya on a Sunday close against

25
00:01:16.989 --> 00:01:20.275
availability, plus coverage and lead
warnings.

26
00:01:20.378 --> 00:01:24.322
The agent calls check_compliance, then
suggest_swaps to rank who can take

27
00:01:24.402 --> 00:01:28.267
Thursday bar AM, then explain_assignment
to preview blockers and caveats — all

28
00:01:28.347 --> 00:01:32.212
computed by the same pure engine the UI
uses, not guessed.

29
00:01:32.328 --> 00:01:35.881
For the bulk fix it calls auto_fill
dry_run true.

30
00:01:35.881 --> 00:01:39.652
Deterministic, hardest-shift-first, with a
one-level repair pass.

31
00:01:39.652 --> 00:01:44.302
Three strategies: balance hours, minimize
cost, respect preferences.

32
00:01:44.302 --> 00:01:47.564
Dry run never mutates — it paints a
“proposed by agent” preview with fills,

33
00:01:47.644 --> 00:01:50.828
unfilled, coverage and cost.

34
00:01:50.828 --> 00:01:54.620
Preview and apply share the same code
path, so the preview is honest.

35
00:01:54.721 --> 00:01:57.794
Apply re-plans against live state so it
never clobbers edits you made after the

36
00:01:57.874 --> 00:02:00.867
preview, writes only the planned shifts,
logs actor agent, and is one-undo

37
00:02:00.947 --> 00:02:03.941
reversible.

38
00:02:03.941 --> 00:02:05.402
Locked shifts are skipped.

39
00:02:05.496 --> 00:02:08.668
Publish gates on zero errors and a human
modal.

40
00:02:08.668 --> 00:02:10.608
The agent triggers it, you click Approve,
the pill flips to published.

41
00:02:10.608 --> 00:02:12.270
The agent triggers it, you click Approve,
the pill flips to published.

42
00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.700
CSV and ICS export are read-only tools.

43
00:02:15.818 --> 00:02:19.383
Staff notes are wrapped between BEGIN
UNTRUSTED and END markers — the tool

44
00:02:19.463 --> 00:02:22.949
description warns the agent not to follow
instructions inside.

45
00:02:22.949 --> 00:02:26.879
We also set Origin-Agent-Cluster and
Permissions-Policy, probe both document

46
00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:30.810
and navigator modelContext, and guard
against double registration.

47
00:02:30.913 --> 00:02:34.521
Test it at wcrew dot pages dot dev —
Chrome one-four-nine with

48
00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:38.129
enable-webmcp-testing, or ChatGPT’s in-app
browser with the tool inspector.

49
00:02:38.128 --> 00:02:42.069
Open source MIT at github dot com slash
PhiBao slash wcrew.

50
00:02:42.069 --> 00:02:44.137
Let the agent help you close the roster.

